From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: sc8280xp: cap Pocket S2 headphone digital volume

The Pocket S2 headphone volume is the RX digital volume: with the WCD939x
compander enabled the HPHL/HPHR PA gain has no effect on the output level.
The control spans -84..+40 dB, so exposing it as the playback volume would
map 100% of the slider to +40 dB. Limit it to 59 (-25 dB) on this board
only: above that the output crackles.

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c b/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
index 00f1a3c..217245f 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
@@ -59,6 +59,18 @@ static int sc8280xp_snd_init(struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd)
 			snd_soc_limit_volume(card, "WSA_RX1 Digital Volume", 71);
 		}
 		break;
+	case RX_CODEC_DMA_RX_0:
+	case RX_CODEC_DMA_RX_1:
+		/*
+		 * Pocket S2 headphones are driven from the RX digital volume
+		 * (the PA gain has no effect with the compander on). Its range
+		 * runs up to +40 dB, so cap it at -25 dB, above which the output crackles.
+		 */
+		if (of_machine_is_compatible("ayaneo,pocket-s2")) {
+			snd_soc_limit_volume(card, "RX_RX0 Digital Volume", 59);
+			snd_soc_limit_volume(card, "RX_RX1 Digital Volume", 59);
+		}
+		break;
 	case DISPLAY_PORT_RX_0:
 		/* DISPLAY_PORT dai ids are not contiguous */
 		dp_pcm_id = 0;
